  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Acer palmatum 'Right Fred' Deep Maroon-Purple Japanese Maple Zones 5-9 Acer palmatum 'Right Fred' is a stunning deciduous tree that is sure to make a statement in any garden or landscape. In the spring, with its upright form and broad shape, this tree is a great choice for adding structure and height to a planting scheme. The leaves of 'Right Fred' are a beautiful purple-red color are accented by prominent dark veins. This gives a nice reticulated \"ghost-like\" variegation on a dark purple leaf. As the fall season arrives, the leaves turn a range of colors from orange to scarlet, providing a stunning display of autumnal hues. To thrive, 'Right Fred' prefers a sunny or partly shaded location with well-drained soil to hold its variegation longer into the season. This cultivar was discovered and introduced by the Flora Wonder™ Collection of Buchholz Nursery, a trusted name in the plant industry. Gardeners will appreciate the beauty and versatility of Acer palmatum 'Right Fred. ' The tree's unique purple coloration and leaf shape make it a standout specimen, whether planted alone or as part of a larger landscape design. 'Right Fred' may reach 6-8 ft in height in 10 years. 'Right Fred' is a relatively low-maintenance tree that requires only moderate watering and pruning to maintain its shape and health."
  },
